James inquired about replacing all instances of "0.36" with "0.53" in a directory tree of R files. I recommended using the `sed` command in a Unix-like terminal, providing a step-by-step command that includes finding all `.R` files, executing `sed` to perform the replacement globally in each file, and emphasized the importance of backing up files first. I also offered an alternative to create backup files by modifying the `sed` command to include a `.backup` extension for original files.
